From cf952cb99d0e3947e2b263a312e310c0e8a722a7 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Ivy Evans <ivy@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 16 Oct 2026 12:31:26 -0700
Subject: [PATCH 6/6] Core: under Wine, do not minimise the game when it loses
 activation

About one start in three under Proton in Steam's Game Mode (Bazzite,
gamescope) stopped on a black screen after the logo movies and never
reached the main menu. Read from the hung process: the main thread was in
SwapBuffers (0x004048C1), inside Mesa's DRI3 back-buffer wait
(loader_dri3_get_buffers -> dri3_find_back -> dri3_wait_for_event_locked
-> xcb_wait_for_special_event), and every other thread was idle. The game
window's Win32 style was 0xB6000000, against 0x96000000 on a good start;
the difference is WS_MINIMIZE. Wine had sized its OpenGL child window to
the minimised client rectangle, 160x31, instead of 1920x1080, and the
X server never released a back buffer for it.

The game minimises itself. Its window procedure (0x00402800) handles
WM_ACTIVATEAPP at 0x00402951; on a deactivation in fullscreen (the render
window's +0xAC, vtable slot 1) it calls ShowWindow(hwnd, SW_MINIMIZE) at
0x004029DB, then restores the gamma ramp and the desktop's mode (slot 6).
On Windows that is how Alt-Tab leaves an exclusive-fullscreen game. In a
compositor with no taskbar nothing restores the window, and the restore
would run on the thread that is waiting in the swap. The logo movie's
window handing over to the game window is what deactivated it; the Steam
and quick-access overlays do not.

Hook the hwnd load before the call (mov ecx, [0x007A39D8], absolute,
nothing to relocate). Under Wine (ntdll exports wine_get_version) the
handler returns 1 and the consumed exit at 0x004029E1 skips the push,
push and call; the gamma and mode restore still run. On Windows it
returns 0 and the original minimise runs. A core hook: it is not the
controller's.

The handler compiles in the Linux build of the standalone module; the
main module that installs it has not been built. The same change, the
call replaced with NOPs in the running game's memory, was played under
Proton: no black screen in the starts since, and the window never showed
WS_MINIMIZE. Issue #6 reported the game minimising during a movie skip.
